This rewrite uses Chromium's WebAuthenticationProxy extension API and a Rust
software WebAuthn signer.
The default software path does not require soft-fido2, UHID, host hidraw access,
new kernel drivers, proprietary Windows Hello, phone-unlock software or hardware
attestation. The separately enabled helper FIDO adapter uses existing OS HID APIs;
the container hook is a userspace FIDO-only ABI adapter, not a kernel USB driver.

